WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.120
Marvel fans are about to get a whole lot more
Thor — and we mean that literally.

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:08.980
At Marvel's 2019 Comic-Con panel, it was announced
that Natalie Portman would reprise her role

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.960
as Jane Foster for Thor: Love and Thunder,
which will see her become the new Thor.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.360
Here's how Portman reacted to the news.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.349
Visibly giddy over the announcement, Portman
took to the Hall H stage to share her feelings

00:00:19.349 --> 00:00:20.769
about being the next Thor.

00:00:20.769 --> 00:00:24.321
She walked across the panel, backed by the
cheers of hundreds of Hall H attendees, to

00:00:24.321 --> 00:00:27.200
accept a prop Mjolnir from director Taika
Waititi.

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:31.640
Clearly, Portman is excited about her character
Jane taking over as the first female Thor

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.060
and the second iteration of the god of thunder
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.260
But she knows what it takes to be a superhero,
and the actress is fully prepared for the

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:42.880
same workouts that transformed Tom Holland
and Brie Larson for their own superheroic

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:43.400
roles.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.280
After Marvel's SDCC presentation, Portman
shared two photos of herself on stage with

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:52.100
Mjolnir, writing that she wants everyone to
remember what she looked like during the panel

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:54.780
so they can compare it to her physique in
Thor: Love and Thunder.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.660
Thor: Love and Thunder takes inspiration from
The Mighty Thor comic series by Jason Aaron

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:03.681
and Russell Dauterman, which turns astrophysicist
Jane Foster into a new iteration of the God

00:01:03.681 --> 00:01:04.360
of Thunder.

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:08.060
At the start of the series, Jane is battling
breast cancer when she learns she can carry

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:12.100
the mystical hammer and take over for Thor
after he loses his ability to wield it.

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.500
In the series, Jane's use of Mjolnir and transformations
into Thor actually exacerbates the side effects

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.100
of her cancer.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.350
It's unclear how much of this arc Thor: Love
and Thunder will adapt, but if they stay true

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.000
to the comic storyline, it might be a pretty
emotional ride.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:29.400
It's also bound to be an action-packed one,
as the female Thor possesses all the same

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.120
abilities the Odinson does as well as something
extra.

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:37.200
In The Mighty Thor, Jane has an extra-keen
dominion over Mjolnir, and can alter its velocity

00:01:37.210 --> 00:01:41.700
and trajectory after she's already thrown
it; she can also round up enemies with Mjolnir

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.700
by sending it swirling around their bodies.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.190
The Mighty Thor mastermind Aaron couldn't
be happier that the female Thor is coming

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:51.720
to the MCU, and is eager to see how Portman
approaches this new side of Jane Foster.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:52.440
He tweeted:

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:53.720
"Well, wow."

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.690
"Consider me thunderously excited.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:02:00.080
The Jane Foster Thor storyline I did with
@rdauterman, (Eisner winner!)

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.189
@COLORnMATT &amp; so many more talented artists
is one of my proudest moments in comics.

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:08.340
I can't wait to see TaikaWaititi &amp; Natalie
Portman bring the Goddess of Thunder to life."

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.190
Whatever your thoughts on Portman becoming
the new Thor are, there's no denying that

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:13.950
this is huge news for the actress.

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:18.290
The last fans saw of her in the MCU was in
Thor: The Dark World, after which she and

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:19.340
Thor broke up off-screen.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.680
Portman herself had also seemingly parted
ways with the Marvel movie world after the

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.860
Thor sequel, telling The Wall Street Journal
in 2016:

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.700
"As far as I know, I'm done."

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.720
Of course, we know now that Portman isn't
through with the MCU — and she may not be

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:32.460
done with Thor, either.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.290
Marvel hasn't said one way or another whether
Jane and Thor will give their relationship

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.940
another shot in Love and Thunder, but we're
betting it's possible.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:42.600
“Sorry to hear Jane dumped you.”

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.100
“She didn’t dump me, you know.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.160
I dumped her.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:47.960
It was a mutual dumping.”

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:52.520
After all, the two are both worthy of wielding
Mjolnir in the eyes of the Asgardian gods.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.320
It seems as if their romance was written in
the stars.

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:59.060
See Natalie Portman's Jane Foster become the
new Thor when Thor: Love and Thunder hits

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.460
theaters on November 5th, 2021.

